@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+# v2 camera zoom + pan (wheel zoom-to-point + drag pan)
+
+**User directive (2026-08-23):** "zoom in and out enabled — to see areas and
+out for the overall bird view of the city." The prerequisite for the
+real-city-maps arc + a standalone UX win.
+
+## What ships
+
+- **Wheel zoom-to-point** — the wheel zooms the map around the cursor (not
+  the window center), clamped to `[1.0 fit, 4.0]` (min = the current
+  fit-to-window bird's view; max = nodes/links read clearly — a 26px design
+  tile renders ~96px, a basic puck ~110px). The 7.1 eased camera model is
+  extended, not replaced: the wheel sets the eased targets; the anchor math
+  keeps the world point under the cursor pinned at the converged frame.
+- **Drag pan** — a left-drag on EMPTY map space pans the camera (clamped to
+  the world rect). The draw gesture only ever begins on a node press, so the
+  empty-ground drag is free — no gesture conflict by construction. Placement
+  mode, tray/popover/QoS swallows, the settings modal, and ESC/right-click
+  frames all keep their existing ownership (pins below).
+- **Wheel ownership vs the NOC panel** — the wheel is the MAP's: the NOC
+  drop log scrolls ONLY while the pointer is over the panel (the r1
+  scroll-clamp surface); anywhere else the wheel zooms (PP_DEBUG-only
+  distinction — release builds always zoom). The old unconditional wheel
+  read in the render block is gone; the policy lives in one place
+  (`effect_zoom`).
+- **HUD + overlays stay screen-space** — the HUD, NOC panel, chips, banners
+  anchor to the window (unchanged); world elements scale with the camera
+  (nodes, wires, packets, terrain, the procedural map).
+- **Two-finger touch pan now works** — the 5.4 `Pan` intent's deliberate
+  no-op is superseded: the executor routes it to the camera (same effect as
+  the mouse drag; FORGE #6 parity by construction).
+
+## Evidence (committed, mechanical)
+
+`docs/captures/v2-camera-zoom/` — the PP_CAM_E2E drive (PP_DEBUG + env-flag,
+the D-lesson pattern): real wheel events + a real empty-ground drag through
+the REAL input pipeline, captured at the default fit and after the
+zoom+pan settle.
+
+| frame | paper (canvas) fraction | note |
+|---|---|---|
+| `zoom-00-fit.png` (default camera) | 24.3% | the camera-fit board margins |
+| `zoom-01-zoomed-panned.png` (4x + pan) | 0.0% | the map fills the window |
+
+61.4% of pixels differ between the two frames; the zoomed frame shows the
+map magnified with a node up close and the HUD intact at screen-space
+(vision-verified via the KYLE model — the standing vision path).
+
+**Zero golden drift:** the harness capture path pins the default camera (it
+never runs `camera_update`), so this job re-blessed NOTHING — `harness run`
+is 48/48 demos green with T1 hashes, T2 pixels, and the replay gate
+byte-identical (the mechanical acceptance: same tick at default zoom matches
+the old captures).
+
+## Verification
+
+- **11/11 local CI gates green** (lint, unit suites ×6 packages, app build,
+  harness T1/T2/replay, palcheck, drift-check, preview-check, motion-pixel,
+  PP_DEBUG builds, stats-check, input-parity 27 scenarios).
+- New pins: 4 camera-math tests (app/render/camera_test.odin) + 4 input
+  wiring tests (app/input/camera_input_test.odin) — the pan/draw/click
+  conflict gates, the wheel chain, and the zoom anchor/clamp math.
+- No golden re-bless, no catalog/serialization touch, no sim change:
+  T1/replay hash-equal by construction (view-layer only).
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **Pan gesture: left-drag on empty ground** (the briefing delegated the
+  choice). Middle/space-drag were NOT needed: the draw gesture starts only on
+  a node press (`Begin_Draw`), so the empty-ground left-drag is unclaimed
+  surface — the natural Mini-Motorways-style pan with zero conflict. The pan
+  latch arms only when the press snaps to NO node, is not swallowed by
+  UI/tray/popover/QoS, and is not in placement mode. A pan release never
+  click-selects (the existing >6px moved-check); a click (no movement) keeps
+  the 5.5 click-select surface exactly.
+- **Text at zoom: snap to screen-space.** The world pass draws NO text; every
+  label (QoS readouts, heat %, node chips) draws at fixed screen sizes via
+  the bilinear-filtered font atlas, anchored to world positions through the
+  live transform. There is no world-space text to scale, so no blurry
+  bitmap scaling exists (rule 6 resolved by construction, documented).
+- **Single-finger touch drag stays tap-select** (no pan): the 5.4 mapping
+  keeps single-touch as draw/tap; two-finger pan (the established touch pan
+  intent) now really pans. Mouse pan + touch two-finger pan share the ONE
+  executor path.
+- **Zoom clamp 4.0** — beyond it sprite-pixel upscaling adds no information;
+  the selection focus (2.3/2.6) sits inside the band.
+- **Eased targets, not instant zoom** — the 7.1 motion-readability ease
+  stays; zoom-to-point anchors against the live transform so the cursor
+  point holds at the converged frame (pin-tested).
+- **Wheel step is integer-notch** (1.25^n via repeated multiply, no libm —
+  the §10.4 rule); smooth-trackpad fractional deltas accumulate per frame
+  and fire whole notches (same truncation the old NOC scroll used).
+- **Panning is clamped to the world rect** — the zoomed-in view can never
+  fly off into the paper void; at the 1.0 fit the center pins (pan is a
+  no-op at the min zoom, by construction).
+- **Missed-release guard**: a pan latch never strands — the poll synthesizes
+  a release when the button is up but the latch is set (focus-loss/missed
+  edge), `begin_draw` clears it, and `start_run` resets it.
+
+## Canon notes
+
+- **bmad-build skill waiver (carried per the 2026-08-21 Silas ruling):** the
+  briefing's Skills policy names `bmad-quick-dev` (→ `bmad-build`), whose
+  render entrypoint (`_bmad/scripts/render_skill.py`) does not exist in this
+  repo. Per the standing field-note ruling (orchestrator-night-watchman,
+  2026-08-21), the skill is WAIVED and this job executed self-contained from
+  the briefing (scope/rules/acceptance were complete); the waiver is carried
+  as this canon note.
+- The 5.4 `Pan` no-op comment is superseded by this story (the camera now
+  pans); the parity pan scenario's contract (no commands) is unchanged.
